ASoC: qcom: audioreach: drive a TDM backend through MODULE_ID_TDM_SINK

The Xiaomi 12 Pro's four CS35L41 amps sit on tertiary TDM. The phone's own
ACDB lists MODULE_ID_TDM_SINK (0x0700100E) as the hardware endpoint for that
port and never mentions I2S_SINK or AUDIO_IF_SINK, and the vendor SPF build
rejects graphs built on either of those. The downstream machine driver runs
it at 8 x 32-bit slots with the TER_TDM_IBIT clock at rate * 32 * 8.

Adds PARAM_ID_TDM_INTF_CFG for TDM_SINK, TDM dai ops (tdm slots, bit clock
vote, format), the TER_TDM_IBIT PRM clock, and the machine-driver setup:
S32 on the backend, slots 0/1, per-amp channel from the sound-name-prefix.
